  "query_preview": "..\n(Friday Night through next Thursday)\nIssued at 1035 AM CST Thu Nov 19 2026\n\nThe weekend will start off nice with the well above average \ntemperatures continuing on Saturday. South winds will increase to 5-\n10 mph on Saturday ahead of our next chance of rain. A trough will \nsweep through the plains on late Saturday into Sunday dragging a \ncold front towards our area. There should be enough moisture and \nlift ahead of the front to produce some scattered showers late \nSunday afternoon into Sunday night. QPF with this system continues \nto look light with rain amounts a quarter inch or less. Cooler \nweather will move in behind the front to start the week with high \ntemperatures back in the 50s on Monday and Tuesday. There will be \nanother trough that moves across the plains late Tuesday into \nWednesday with plenty of uncertainty with the track of that system. \nDepending on the track, we may see another chance of rain on \nWednesday.",
